1. She holds a master's degree. (Verbatim: "i got my master's degree i got a master's degree let me let me let me use my fancy play part")

2. She previously worked in IT jobs and in an office environment. (Verbatim: "when i was doing my it jobs um it was a lot of work really really hard")

3. She used to work intensely for short periods and then rest, describing her approach as "min maxing." (Verbatim: "i'd work really hard for like one or two hours and then be like okay i'm done like i'll work hard to reward myself with the nap")

4. She introduced Cookie Clicker to her entire office, causing a productivity drop and competitive clicking. (Verbatim: "i accidentally got my entire office into cookie clicker... now no one can judge my clicking because everybody's clicking")

5. She has a lazy approach to using her intelligence and admits to not liking to think when she can avoid it. (Verbatim: "i'm pretty lazy when it comes to my brain i can tell when i'm not using it and it's a lot of the time")

6. She believes most workers are only productive around 10% of the time, sometimes less. (Verbatim: "the average human worker is productive like 50% of the time oh damn that's a high number um i'm gonna go for like 10% of the time")

7. She was once managed by a supportive boss who encouraged rest and self-care. (Verbatim: "my manager was like you always get all your work done... but you're allowed to not do work for a bit you can relax")

8. She watched anime, specifically Love Live, during work hours. (Verbatim: "i ended up starting to watch anime um yeah in my in my like at work um but that was the same place where i thought it was safe to watch love live on my phone")

