1. She has a deeply embarrassing memory of practicing a dance in a bathroom mirror at work, being caught by a coworker, and curling into a ball on the floor out of shame. (Verbatim: "I froze and I felt like it stopped and I just turned and then I dropped to the floor and and and just like curled up in a ball to hide... she didn't say anything that's the worst part she didn't say a word.")

2. Her ability to act as an extrovert online stems from overcoming intense embarrassment and social shame in real life. (Verbatim: "extrovert Ellie exists through the shame and embarrassment that I've gone through where I'm like okay it's not as bad as that time I can cope with this.")

3. She describes herself as “fueled by cringe” and embraces being seen as embarrassing, claiming “cringe runs through my veins.” (Verbatim: "I'm fueled by cringe runs through my veins and I live off copium and trauma.")

4. She maintains a “normie disguise” in real life, successfully blending in with regular society so well that coworkers have no idea she is a VTuber. (Verbatim: "my co-workers think I'm a regular person the disguise is working... they would never guess in a million years I was an anime girl on the internet.")

5. She refers to her time pretending to be a regular person in society as her “normie arc.” (Verbatim: "I had my normie arc and it was such a good yeah the normie disc.")

6. She uses dark humor that is well-received in certain circles but causes concern when used around “normie” friends who misinterpret it as a sign of depression. (Verbatim: "when my dark like humor slips out... you should have seen the look of concern on their face when they were like ellia are you okay?")

7. She jokes about wanting to be “isekai’d by a truck,” indicating familiarity with anime tropes, though it causes alarm among non-anime fans. (Verbatim: "I want to get isekai'd by a truck I'm like what the heck is isekai why a truck like what do you mean... concern concern concern absolute concern.")

8. She struggles with setting alarms and ringtones because she fears associating music she likes with anxiety or dread. (Verbatim: "I'm scared that whatever ringtone... will then become anxiety inducing... same with an alarm if i set anything to my alarm that noise will then become associated with the anxiety of waking up.")

9. She once had an embarrassing moment when her phone alarm played an anime dragon greeting at full volume in the office, drawing stares. (Verbatim: "my alarm going off with an anime dragon's good morning mother... office folk turned their head and stared.")

10. She has a recurring habit of making a heart shape with her hands when saying “look love,” even if viewers can’t see it. (Verbatim: "every hecking time I say look love I make the heart shape with my hand.") [end of text]



