1. She was called "sparrow" by her father ("papa elia") because she ate like a sparrow and there were many sparrows where she grew up. (Verbatim: "papa elia would always call me um a sparrow yeah... because i would always eat like a sparrow and there was a lot of... sparrows where i where i lived um growing up")

2. She grew up with two cats, one of which frequently brought live sparrows into the house, which she had to rescue and release. (Verbatim: "i grew up with two cats and one cat would um always bring in sparrows... i used to have to just pick up the sparrow put it outside and be like go be free")

3. She identifies strongly with birds, and her online community has given her the nickname "goose," which has become a significant part of her persona. (Verbatim: "then you go into my place and you're like wow that's a lot of goose stuff looks at two meter goose... the thing that you guys have given me that i didn't choose is is goose")

4. Her family has bird-related themes: her father likes owls, her younger brother is obsessed with ducks, and she herself is associated with sparrows and geese. (Verbatim: "papa ellia's thing is owls... my little brother he's got tons of duck things... and then you go into my place and you're like wow that's a lot of goose stuff")

5. She considers herself a cat person and had a black-and-white cat she deeply loved, which used to sleep with her every night. (Verbatim: "i'm a cat person um yeah absolutely... my cat would sleep under the duvet and then as I got older... it then moved to sort of sleeping half under the duvet")

6. Her cat had a permanently grumpy-looking face but was actually happy and chill, though others often called it ugly. (Verbatim: "everybody would always call my cat really ugly... he had this sort of face that sort of like said like I give up... but he never gave up to be honest he was actually quite a fighter")

